---
id: AP-004
type: rule
family: guardrail-suppression
title: '@ts-ignore suppresses all errors'
version: 1

severity: warning
confidence: high
spectrum_position: 1

targets: [source]
file_extensions: [.ts, .tsx]
allowlist: ['**/*.test.ts', '**/*.spec.ts', '**/__tests__/**', '**/explain/**']

detection:
  type: regex
  pattern: '@ts-ignore'

related: [AP-005, AP-001]
enabled: true
opt_in: false
---

Don't suppress this TypeScript error — fix it. Read the actual error
message and address the type mismatch directly.

If you must suppress, use `@ts-expect-error` instead. It fails when the
underlying issue is resolved, so it's self-cleaning. `@ts-ignore` is
permanent and silences all errors on the next line, including future
ones you don't know about yet.
